# Whether every side of the pair stands at a set of joint positions (ADR-0070).
#
# Asked by the fixed program before its first cycle, and by `./scripts/home`,
# for the program's start: every arm joint at the program's first pose. The
# program reads its OWN domain's joint states, which through the twin are the
# plant's; the counterpart's are on a domain it never opens (ADR-0044 clause 3).
# So it asks the boundary, which already reads every side's joint states.
#
# The sides named in `sides` are judged - a target's own (ADR-0072) - or, with
# none named, every side the deployment runs, in every mode: this is a
# measurement before anything is commanded, not a question about the sides a
# mode commands (contrast TrackArrived). The boundary answers a verdict and not the positions:
# the reverse state flow is consumed by L5 and republished nowhere (ADR-0050
# decision 1b). A physical side's position counts only while it is fresh (the
# plan's `state_max_age_s`, on the boundary's steady clock); one not heard, or
# too old, is UNHEARD.
#
# SERVICE is the one place this name is written, as SetMode's is.

string SERVICE="/cite/twin/joints_at"

string[] joints     # joint names, as the plan names them
float64[] positions # the target of each joint, in the joint's own unit, same order
float64 tolerance   # one tolerance for every joint, in the joints' own unit
string[] sides      # the sides to judge, by the plan's side names (ADR-0072); empty
                    # judges every side the deployment runs, as before. A side named
                    # that does not run is UNHEARD
---
# Why `at` is what it is. AWAY outranks UNHEARD, as in TrackArrived.
uint8 AT=0          # every side stands within tolerance of every target
uint8 AWAY=1        # a side heard (fresh, if physical) stands outside the tolerance
uint8 UNHEARD=2     # none is AWAY, but a side's joint is not heard, or too old
uint8 MALFORMED=3   # no joints, a count mismatch, or a negative tolerance

bool at             # reason == AT
uint8 reason        # one of the constants above
string detail       # which side's joint is where; or why none counts
